WEBVTT

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.250
So, you'll be returning home soon, Lowa?

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.670
Yes, but this was a very fruitful trip.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.090
I only regret

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:20.340
that I was unable to secure
your help in seizing the throne.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.100
Yeah, right.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.600
I know you're up to something.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.930
You say the most outlandish things.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.980
So, why do <i>you </i>think I'm here?

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.730
To catch up with old friends?

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.650
So you've no intention of coming clean.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.570
I've no doubt that come spring,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:45.450
there will be a mass uprising among
the alliance nations the empire conquered.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.500
You came here to prevent that.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.460
My goodness.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.420
Whatever gave you that idea?

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.710
Something clicked when I saw
all those weapons here in Natra.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:59.130
They were made in the lands to the west.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.930
Natra is the transit point.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:05.140
But this is just a small cache you're
gathering back home in case of civil war.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:08.180
The weapons made
in the empire are the finest.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.940
But they'll run short if
my brothers fight over them.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.860
So is it not natural to
seek weapons from the west?

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:19.650
Not if they have been so equally divided.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.740
What's this?

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.700
It may be possible to conceal the
movement of small numbers of weapons

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.870
but not this many.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.540
A check of the ledgers kept by arms
merchants that deal with the empire

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.380
revealed the weapons were equally
distributed among three factions.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.590
Keep factional power balanced to prolong
the struggle between the three princes.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.260
That leaves an opening for rebellions
to spark across the empire.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.100
That's the scheme
behind the scenes, isn't it?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:49.890
If I knew about that,
shouldn't I be warning my brothers?

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.890
You probably did.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.770
But they ignored you.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:04:00.360
You're a girl and the youngest sibling,
so your political clout is next to zero.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.700
Realizing you couldn't rely on
your three brothers, you rolled the dice.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:08.740
You'd have one of the rebel
factions revolt before the others,

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.370
and thereby get solid
evidence to show your brothers.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.920
And you set the stage for that in...

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.170
...Natra and Gairan province next door.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:21.510
That's where Marquess Antgatal
has his stronghold.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.430
Oh, bother. I'm simply no match for you.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.720
It's basically as you said.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.600
I got wind of the scheme,
but I couldn't persuade my brothers.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.440
Since I couldn't resolve the matter alone,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.020
I thought I'd use myself
as bait to thwart it.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:43.400
Bait? You mean your claim
to the imperial throne?

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.660
If the rebellion succeeds,
the princes will be put to death.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.870
And if the victor captures you,

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.000
they can claim the
imperial fortune and throne.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.330
They may even be able to declare
their nation as the new empire.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.250
After considering which rebel faction
was most likely to take the bait,

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.050
I zeroed in on Marquees Antgatal.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:06.720
He betrayed the alliance
and joined the empire,

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.050
so he would want some powerful backing.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.430
I'd be an attractive pawn for him.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:15.600
I figured it would be easier for him
to get ahold of me if I came here.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.650
You expected Antgatal and
Natra would butt heads over this,

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.940
but what if I said
I'd hand you over to him?

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.150
You'd never do that.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.150
Why not?

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.820
Because of Ninym.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:31.740
If you hand me over,
and the rebellion succeeds,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.250
the west's influence will swell.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:38.000
Then Natra will be caught
between a rock and a hard place.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.340
Unlike the east,
the west treats Flahms like slaves,

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:45.050
so you would never side with them.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:46.970
That explains it.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:51.220
I'm glad to see
you're still by Wein's side.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:55.640
I didn't know why you'd say that
to Ninym, but now it makes sense.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.890
I've nothing left to hide.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:03.650
I imagine Marquees Antgatal's forces
will soon attack Natra to claim my hand.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:07.860
I would have you thwart him
so that I can save the empire.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.780
Did I disappoint you?

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:14.080
After all, I claim to be a friend yet use
you and yours for the empire's sake.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.210
Not at all. That's the Lowa Felbis
I know and love.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.960
However,

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:24.170
will Antgatal's army <i>really </i>invade?

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:26.630
Don't tell me you anticipated that, too?

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.680
As if. I merely sent
the marquees a letter.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:31.640
A letter?

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.850
That's right.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.640
It reads, "A certain noble personage
who has been visiting Natra

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:42.190
will be proceeding to Marquees Antgatal's
manor when they leave."

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.610
When did you...?

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.280
He planned to invade
Natra because you were here.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.700
But if you come to him
without any effort on his part,

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.570
he won't have to attack.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:58.250
Sorry, but you'll have to find
another way to thwart the rebellion.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.540
I see.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:03.460
But I wouldn't be surprised
if Ninym burst through that door

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:06.630
and announced that you're being invaded.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.630
Not gonna happen! Care to bet?

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:13.180
There's no way Antgatal
is going to invade!

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.010
Your Highness!

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:17.350
Forgive me for interrupting.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:20.480
I bring urgent news that cannot wait!

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:27.900
It's a pleasure to make
your acquaintance, Prince Wein.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:33.110
I'm Grenache Antgatal's son,
Gerard Antgatal.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:37.120
What a pleasant surprise.
It's so nice to meet you, Lord Gerard.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.370
I bid you welcome.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:42.120
It's the least you could do.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.960
We are a bit surprised
by the sudden visit.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:48.710
What brings you here?

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:53.050
Obviously, I'm here for
my beautiful flower and future wife,

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:56.470
Princess Lowellmina.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:59.810
At last, Her Highness knows
my true feelings for her!

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:04.190
That's why you sent me
that letter, isn't it, boy?!

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.270
Boy?

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:08.110
I see. So that explains why you are here.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:10.610
Your love has sparked a burning passion.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.320
So, where is my princess
I've awaited so long?!

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.120
Or do you seek to play games with me?!

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.120
If you'd kindly wait,
we have a room ready for you.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.620
You may relax there.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:27.040
Would it not be best to allow
the princess time to be at her loveliest?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.420
You have a point.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:32.880
Wonderful. Tonight, we shall hold
a banquet in honor of the future couple.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.720
Very well. Show me to my room.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:43.520
My son is a fool.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.650
I didn't even have a chance to stop him.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:51.820
Still, if we can pluck the empire's
flower without dispatching our forces...

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:57.530
Your little ruse to topple the empire
may no longer serve any purpose, Owl.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:03.250
I beg your pardon, my lord,
but the rebellion plot is well underway.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.870
This calls for your prudent judgment.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:07.540
Yes, I know!

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:10.750
Let us wait for the
Natran prince's next move.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.800
The groundwork for civil war
has already been laid.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.800
This is a serious obstacle.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:19.220
Damn you, Wein Salema Arbalest!

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:23.270
Sheesh, the power of love
is a curious thing, but...

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:25.600
Why'd he have to come here?!

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.440
Who does that?! Who just shows up
at the palace of a neighboring land?!

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:31.820
He wasn't invited!

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.740
Am I right, Nin--?

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:37.700
He looked down on you the entire time.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.580
Well, he <i>is </i>the heir to
the imperial title of marquess.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:43.750
It's not a big--

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.540
I don't like it, any of it.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.080
I-I know. You're right.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:52.800
But should you really be
getting so angry over this?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.470
After all, anger usually
ends up screwing things up.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:59.010
So let's think happy thoughts!

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.720
Happy thoughts?

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.390
Well, think about me or...

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:05.850
I'll do that.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.810
N-Ninym?

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:11.770
Don't mind me.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.980
Y-Yes, but...

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.990
I thought the letter
would arrive too late.

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:20.450
But at least they didn't
launch an invasion force.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.990
I figured they'd agonize over
the matter till the last minute.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:29.120
Grenache Antgatal isn't the sort of man
who can make such momentous decisions.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:33.250
Lowa's trying to pit
Natra against Antgatal, isn't she?

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:36.970
If so, do you think she'll
try to sabotage the banquet?

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:41.430
No. Now that it's come to this,
she'll use Gerard to her advantage.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:43.350
Using her hand in marriage as bait,

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:46.600
she'll lure him into telling
her about the rebellion.

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:49.350
Marry that pig?!
Even Lowa wouldn't go that far!

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:52.940
You know she'll do anything
to achieve her ends.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.900
And there's more to her plan.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:56.990
There's more?

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:00.280
She likely believes
she has Natra on her side,

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:04.080
so she's dead serious
about taking the imperial throne.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.580
I don't follow.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.370
Lowa wants to save the empire.

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:10.620
Of course she wants
to thwart the rebellion.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:15.170
But she also wants to see her dream
of reigning as empress come true.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:18.670
Lowa has two desires
within her pretty little head.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:23.550
Even if she gets Natra to side with her,
what about the succession battle?

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.510
We lack the power to intervene.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:29.730
But she can show that
she has our political backing

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:33.230
along with her resourcefulness
and grit to save her homeland.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:35.690
Either one alone has little effect,

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:38.940
but together, it's a
different story, don't you think?

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:40.820
I see your point.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:44.530
Her scheme succeeds
if she gets our backing.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.040
But it fell apart, didn't it?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.660
If she ensnares Gerard,

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:52.040
Antgatal will no longer have
a reason to invade Natra.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.630
Right. Which is why she's,
no doubt, attempting the opposite.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:57.250
The opposite?

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:58.880
Most likely...

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:02.970
Have Gerard put down
his father's rebellion?!

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.180
Yes.

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:05.510
It goes like this.

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:07.640
Gerard discovers his father's plot

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.480
while he happens to be
in a neighboring kingdom.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:14.100
There, he tells the imperial princess
about the plot after they grow close.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:18.650
Once the princess learns of the plot,
she helps Gerard take down the rebel.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.110
How does that sound?

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:25.570
But, Your Highness, our troops
and Lord Gerard's followers are few.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.080
How can you take down Grenache Antgatal?

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.910
Our numbers <i>are </i>lacking.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.790
So let's borrow Natra's troops.

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.420
I bet that's what Lowa is thinking.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.000
But give me a break!

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:41.550
No way in hell I'll get our military
involved in an imperial succession war!

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:46.640
So what we need to do now is support
Lowa in manipulating Gerard

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.600
but not lend any troops
in taking down Antgatal.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:54.390
Wein's likely thinking along those lines,
but he's got another thing coming.

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:58.400
He believes Gerard
might become my husband,

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.780
so he has to bring us together here.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:05.240
I imagine he's doing everything in
his power to take advantage of Gerard.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:09.370
But I'll catch him off guard
and make him pledge his troops.

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:10.700
Unbelievable.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.660
Lowa really got us
mixed up in something big.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.250
She really did it this time.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.130
I thought I had him backed into a corner.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:20.960
Wein never fails to impress.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:26.180
--But the last one laughing will be... me!
--But the last one laughing will be... me!

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.260
Quite impressive, Lord Gerard!

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:33.730
Your insight is truly a marvel!

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:37.480
That one such as milord
has yet to take center stage

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:40.320
is a major loss for the empire.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.530
You embarrass me with such high praise.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.410
I simply stated a fact.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:50.530
I am not one to engage in false flattery.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:52.490
Really? You don't say!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.460
Princess Lowellmina,

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:02.800
if you and Lord Gerard are to wed,
it is a momentous event for the empire.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:06.420
Is it not your duty to announce
your betrothal at once?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:10.140
Team up with Gerard, already,
and go crush the rebellion plot!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:14.970
In that case, would you not
travel with us to the empire?

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:18.730
After all, it was you who brought
Lord Gerard and me together.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:23.440
I want everyone to see
that I have Natra's backing.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:28.950
I have the distinct feeling you
two are old acquaintances.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:32.580
Yes, we met when I went
abroad to study in the empire.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.330
Really? When you studied abroad?

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:38.670
So, what was life like while
you lived in the empire?

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:44.550
I am embarrassed to say I spent my days
at an estate and spent my leisure fencing.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.340
You can handle a blade?

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.720
Well, I suppose you could say that.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.470
What a coincidence!

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:55.220
I'm well acquainted with swordplay myself!

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.350
Like hell you are!

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:58.940
What say you?

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:03.360
Shall we dazzle Princess Lowellmina
with our sword skills?

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.280
Seriously?!

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.820
Why not humor the poor slob?

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:10.780
Easier said than done!

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:12.620
Have fun! Good luck!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.370
God damn it!

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.580
And the rules are?

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:27.090
Whoever knocks the other's sword
out of his hands wins.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:34.720
This won't even be close, but...

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:40.480
Prince Wein is the perfect foil
to make me look good.

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:42.560
He really thinks he can win?!

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:46.020
I've got to make Gerard look good.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:49.360
However, I have my
own reputation to maintain.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:51.360
I can't lose without a fight.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:55.240
After crossing blades for a bit,
I'll make a move when he's winded.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:16:01.000
I'll knock the sword out of his hand
and drop mine so it ends in a draw!

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:11.300
Now!

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.300
Whoops!

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.430
What the...?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.310
Look out!

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:28.480
The prince is a marvel!

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:33.150
Oh, no, I won!

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:36.660
Why'd you have to go and win?!

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:40.290
It's not too late. I'll just drop
my sword on purpose.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.370
Your Highness!

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:47.590
This is bad! What now?!

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:52.300
On top of being defeated,
Gerard will also be seen as a dirty cheat!

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.340
I can't prevent or parry his blow!

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:57.180
I'll just have to dodge!

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:01.310
But it's got to be so natural that
no one thinks I did it on purpose.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.810
Damn, I'm good.

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.290
Wait. What?

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:27.420
Lord Gerard?!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:30.550
Ninym, is Lord Gerard okay?!

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:33.800
Well, I don't know how to put this.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.680
I am afraid to even say it.

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:38.300
He is deceased.

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:41.350
What?

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:43.140
Gerard is...

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.640
...dead?!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.100
His squire just arrived
with the terrible news

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.520
that Lord Gerard fell to his death
from the Natran palace.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:53.490
This cannot be! It must be a mistake!

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:56.030
But his squire brought this.

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:57.780
That is Gerard's...

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:02.990
His squire said the rest of the retinue
was taken captive by the Natrans.

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:05.660
Only he escaped, and just barely at that.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.460
Where is this squire?

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:11.170
He was so weak and exhausted,
we're having him rest.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:15.300
Find out everything that transpired
as soon as he wakes.

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:16.880
Yes, my lord!

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:25.390
What possibly could have happened?

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:27.770
An illness? An accident?

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:31.310
Or could it have been... murder?!

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:34.190
Yes, my son must have been murdered!

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:38.610
Now we have good reason to invade Natra.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:41.990
And Princess Lowellmina...

00:18:41.990 --> 00:18:45.870
No, the letter we received
was in the prince's name,

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:48.830
but it did announce
the princess's intentions.

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.500
It means but one thing

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.920
if the prince's letter
was issued with her consent.

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:58.340
The princess must have been
involved in this assassination.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:05.020
Could it be that she caught wind of
the rebellion plot against the empire?!

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.930
The timing couldn't have been worse.

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:12.940
War between Natra and Antgatal will
inevitably attract too much attention.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:17.280
We must avoid anything that draws
undue scrutiny during our planning stage.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.030
Change of plans!

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:21.450
Gather our sources within the manor!

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:22.490
Yes, sir!

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:30.420
With all due respect, Your Highness,
should we not consider returning home now?

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:31.750
Why?

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:38.420
I am aware of Your Highness's plan to
save the empire and ascend to the throne.

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:43.300
But remaining here any longer
poses a threat to your person.

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:44.760
Fyshe...

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:47.970
Fyshe!

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:51.270
Your Highness? What are you...?

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:56.360
I've always dreamed of having
my very own retainer who I can trust.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:20:01.530
Until now, I never had anyone
I could think of in that way.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.700
Don't be silly.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.620
Time is of the essence.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.120
Yes, I know.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:12.210
Every word of your wise counsel is sound.

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:16.000
My life is at risk if
I remain here any longer.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:21.840
However, my life means little
in the grand scheme of things.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:24.340
I'm in no position
to ascend to the throne.

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:29.430
Therefore, as an imperial princess and
loyal subject who loves her homeland,

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:33.060
peace within the empire
must be my prime objective.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:38.320
Let's say that a suspicious
letter suddenly lured

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.740
a major noble's son
to a neighboring kingdom.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:42.700
All right.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:44.660
And then said son dies.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:45.490
All right.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:47.700
What will people think?

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:49.950
That he was assassinated, no doubt.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.910
I know! Right?!

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:54.870
Why'd you have to
kick the bucket, Gerard?!

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.290
You had to challenge me
to a mock sword duel!

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.300
Then you lost the duel <i>and </i>your temper,

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:02.130
charged through a window,
fell, and broke your neck.

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:03.930
Who the hell does that?!

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:06.430
I never saw <i>that </i>coming.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:07.890
The way things are going,

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:11.810
it'll mean war with Antgatal,
not to mention the empire.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:16.230
I was just trying to get Gerard and
Lowa engaged so they'd go home!

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:18.110
All right, calm down.

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:21.780
We'll just preempt whatever
move Marquees Antgatal makes.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:22.900
You're right.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:26.780
All our motives...
mine, Lowa's, and Antgatal's

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:29.200
have collided in one
big tangled, flaming mess.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:34.500
Whoever seizes the initiative now
will have a huge advantage!

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.880
Pardon me, Your Highness.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:40.090
Princess Lowellmina has
requested an urgent meeting.

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:41.710
What shall I say?

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:42.800
Show her in.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.840
Highness.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.720
She stole the initiative.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:50.430
Oh, no! I haven't even
figured out Lowa's next move!

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:54.600
Do you suppose she'll protest
the death of a noble of the empire?

00:21:54.600 --> 00:22:00.070
If so, she'll make some sort of demand.

00:22:00.070 --> 00:22:01.730
Her Highness is here.

00:22:01.730 --> 00:22:04.650
He could've at least taken his time!

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:06.570
Greetings, Princess Lowellmina.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:11.240
Thank you for taking the time
to meet with me, Prince Wein.

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:15.370
My door and Natra's are
always open to you, Your Highness.

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:18.830
I shall be brief.

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:20.090
I surrender.

00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:21.590
Huh?!

00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:25.130
I was pushing my luck,
which was arrogant of me.

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:29.930
But I've given up trying to use
this incident to rise to the top.

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:34.140
From now on, I intend
to focus on crushing the rebellion.

00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:38.440
As such, would you not
help me devise a plan?

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:42.610
Antgatal can muster
no more than 4,000 troops.

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:45.690
Gairan province as a whole
can likely muster twice that.

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:48.990
That's a reasonable estimate
of Antgatal's strength.

00:22:48.990 --> 00:22:51.660
They're using arms
and armor from the west.

00:22:51.660 --> 00:22:55.500
But they're short on commanders,
and those they have aren't that good.

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:58.250
That's right. They also
don't have enough horses.

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:01.840
If it comes to war,
their army will be mainly on foot.

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:03.920
Yes, <i>if </i>it comes to war.

00:23:03.920 --> 00:23:06.970
Wein, don't tell me
you've suddenly grown soft?

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:08.760
As if!

00:23:08.760 --> 00:23:12.510
I have a far simpler reason
for avoiding this war.

00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:13.890
Frankly, we're broke!

00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:15.020
What?

00:23:15.020 --> 00:23:18.810
Our current budget will only
allow us to muster about 500 troops.

00:23:18.810 --> 00:23:20.060
Surely you jest.

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:22.190
I'm dead serious.

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:24.860
We've yet to recover
from our war with Marden.

00:23:24.860 --> 00:23:26.280
Right, Ninym?

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:29.400
Yes. Mustering any more troops will have

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:32.570
a negative impact on
the political situation here.

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:37.330
And I'm not about to face an
army of 4,000 with just 500 troops.

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:41.920
I see. It makes sense
that you'd wish to avoid war.

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:46.500
But if there is no military solution,
how do you propose we resolve this?

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:51.180
Is defeating Grenache militarily
truly our objective?

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:52.340
It's not, is it?

00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:55.390
We want to hear him
confess about the rebellion

00:23:55.390 --> 00:23:57.850
so a mass uprising never happens.

00:23:57.850 --> 00:24:03.980
We've been pulling off impossible feats
like this ever since our academy days.

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:09.190
Now then, let's get cracking
on our devious scheme!
